\begin{abstract}
This proposal describes a Bangla-language chatbot running on a Raspberry Pi.
Users type (and optionally speak) questions in Bangla and receive Bangla answers
from a local knowledge base, without depending on a cloud service. The project
follows an Iterative-Incremental process over 15 weeks and produces a working
prototype, UML documentation, tests, and a user manual.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction}
Most chatbots serve English speakers well, while Bangla speakers (over 230 million
people) have few lightweight, offline-capable tools. A Raspberry Pi is cheap, small,
and suitable for schools, libraries, and help desks. This project builds a
Bangla Q\&A assistant that runs entirely on it.

\section{Problem Statement}
Existing assistants have weak Bangla support, need constant internet, and run on
expensive hardware. There is no low-cost, offline, Bangla-first assistant for
small institutions.

\section{Objectives}
\begin{itemize}[noitemsep]
  \item Build a chatbot that understands and replies in Bangla.
  \item Run it on a Raspberry Pi (Raspberry Pi OS, Python 3).
  \item Store conversations and a knowledge base in SQLite.
  \item Provide a simple GUI and an admin way to extend the knowledge base.
  \item (Optional) Add Bangla speech input/output.
\end{itemize}

\section{Scope}
\textbf{In scope:} text chat in Bangla, rule/keyword-based intent matching,
FAQ-style domain (e.g.\ campus information), conversation history, admin editing of answers.\\
\textbf{Out of scope:} large language models, multi-language support, mobile app,
cloud deployment.

