\section{Feasibility Study}
\textbf{Technical:} Python, Tkinter, and SQLite run well on Raspberry Pi 4.
\textbf{Economic:} Total hardware cost is low (see Section~\ref{sec:budget}).
\textbf{Operational:} Simple GUI, no training needed for users.
\textbf{Schedule:} 15 weeks is sufficient for the defined scope.

\section{Requirements}
\subsection{Functional Requirements}
\begin{enumerate}[noitemsep]
  \item FR1: User can type a Bangla question and receive a Bangla answer.
  \item FR2: System tokenizes and normalizes Bangla text.
  \item FR3: System matches the question to a knowledge-base entry.
  \item FR4: System shows a fallback reply when no match is found.
  \item FR5: System saves every message with a timestamp.
  \item FR6: Admin can add, edit, and delete knowledge entries.
  \item FR7: User can give feedback (helpful / not helpful).
\end{enumerate}
\subsection{Non-Functional Requirements}
Response time under 2 seconds; correct Bangla Unicode display; runs on 2 GB RAM;
modular code (each class has one responsibility); works offline.

\section{Methodology: Iterative-Incremental Model}
Each increment delivers working software and goes through
requirements $\rightarrow$ design $\rightarrow$ implementation $\rightarrow$ testing.
This suits the project because the NLP part needs repeated tuning with real
test sentences, and early increments give feedback for later ones.

\section{System Architecture}
Layers: (1) Presentation: \texttt{ChatUI}; (2) Logic: \texttt{ChatBot}, \texttt{BanglaNLP};
(3) Data: \texttt{KnowledgeBase}, \texttt{ChatRepository} (SQLite).
\textbf{Hardware:} Raspberry Pi 4 (2/4 GB), microSD 32 GB, display, keyboard,
optional USB microphone and speaker.
\textbf{Software:} Raspberry Pi OS, Python 3, Tkinter, SQLite3, Git, Noto Sans Bengali font.

